                <pb facs="1026" n="932" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg932"/>

                <head>No. 564.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Buck
                        to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-03-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 19, 1887</date>. (Received April
                        14)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 216.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith inclose copy of a note received
                    on the 9th instant from the foreign office, with a translation and a copy of my
                    reply.</p>
                <p>The purpose of this request from the minister was to obtain information in aid of
                    the tax assessor or collector in carrying into effect a law of contributions
                    passed by the last Congress. Under this (in view of the decentralization law
                    which was finally enacted, placing the obligation on the provinces and
                    departments of their own support and management of their fiscal affairs—see
                    relative to said act my No. 142, of August 20, 1866), among other things, a poll
                    or head tax has been imposed.</p>
                <p>I also inclose a copy of the decree of the sub-prefect of Lima, published March
                    3, and translation. I think a note similar to that I inclose from the foreign
                    office has been sent to all the legations here.</p>
                <p>I have, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. W. Buck.</hi></signed></closer>





